WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.167
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:04.601
As you know, we're always
striving to get better

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:06.167
here at "The Tonight Show."

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:09.601
♪ Harder, better,
faster, stronger ♪

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:14.100
So, before every show,
we put out a suggestion box

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.767
for the audience
just to get some feedback

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.334
about what you guys
think of the show,

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.367
things you'd like to see us do,
that kind of stuff.

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.567
So tonight, let's look inside
the Audience Suggestion Box!

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:27.334
-♪ Look into the box,
Audience Suggestion Box ♪

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.067
-There we go.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.934
This first one
is from Erica Dennis.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:35.267
I knew that
before I looked at the card.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:36.868
Yeah, it's from Erica Dennis
right here.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:38.534
Says, "Hey, Jimmy,
in the movie 'Scream,'

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.734
we always assume Drew Barrymore
is talking to the killer,

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:44.934
but can you show us who
she was actually talking to?"

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:47.300
Well, I did some digging,
and we finally got the answer.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.601
Take a look at this.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:51.000
[ Telephone rings ]

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.300
-Hello?
-Can you hear me now?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.434
-Yes.

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:58.200
Can you hear me now?
-Yes.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.234
-Can you hear me now?
-Listen, ass [bleep]!

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:02.901
-Can you hear me now?

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.734
-Is this some kind of joke?

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.167
-Can you hear me now?

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.901
-You've had your fun now,
so I think

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.400
you better just leave or else.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.767
-Can you hear me now?

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.868
-Oh, God!

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.701
-There you go.
Yeah, that makes sense.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.367
There you go.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:19.601
Try another one. This one's
from Claire Martindale.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:22.834
"Hey, Jimmy, you should juggle
those pumpkins on your desk.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:25.000
No cap."

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.567
I haven't really juggled
in a while.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.601
So I --

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:32.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
No, I don't want to...

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.400
I used to.
I don't do it anymore.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.868
[ Audience chanting "Do it!" ]

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:40.234
♪♪

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:45.167
I -- I get a little...
I get a little shy.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:48.901
I get a little shy
when I juggle.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:52.367
So...I'm just gonna -- Ooh.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.534
I'm just gonna -- I'm gonna
turn around and do it.

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:56.667
Can I get a little
juggling music, please?

00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:00.400
[ Funky music plays ]

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.234
♪♪

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:12.067
♪♪

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:14.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.734
-Oh, my God.

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:19.534
Oh, yeah. Fallon for 2!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.367
[ Pop! ]

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:25.801
Wow. Alright. Here we go.

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:28.133
This one is from Sara Dorfman.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.968
"Hey, Jimmy, I love the
'Macarena' challenge on TikTok.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.834
I also love
horror-movie characters.

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.601
Any way you can combine
the two?"

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.200
That's a great idea.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.300
Well, joining us now to do
the "Macarena" challenge,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.400
please welcome
Michael Myers, Pennywise,

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.567
Jason, Freddy Krueger,
and Ghostface!

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:48.234
[ "Macarena" plays ]

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:53.934
♪♪

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:59.601
♪♪

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:01.968
-♪ Hey, Macarena ♪
-♪ Ay ♪

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:04.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.934
♪♪

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:09.968
-Give it up for
the "Macarena" movie monsters!

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:13.200
Not bad! Love those guys.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.567
[ Applause ]

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:20.200
Uh, okay. This one is from
Ryan Taylor Williams.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.868
"Hey, Jimmy, everyone knows
October 31st is Halloween,

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.334
but a lot of people don't know

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:26.634
that it's also
National Magic Day.

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:27.934
You should celebrate that, too."

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.934
Actually, I didn't know that,
but you're in luck,

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:32.267
because I just got word that
there's a magician backstage.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:33.634
His name is the Great Benito,

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:35.467
and we've had him
on the show before.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.434
He's usually pretty good.
Benito, come on out!

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.901
The Great Benito! Benito.

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:41.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:43.801
Ohh! Wow!

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:45.467
Already I'm enjoying this.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.133
Hi. Welcome, Benito.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:50.834
-Hello. Hello there.
Hello there, Jih-- Jih--

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:54.667
I'm getting a J.
Jih-- Jih-- Jury duty?

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.367
-Is this your trick?

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:59.634
-Oh, no, no. No, no. My trick
is much better than that.

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:03.868
-Oh.
-My trick involves this, Jimmy.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:07.267
If that's your real name.
Take a look at this.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.467
-What is that?

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:11.067
-A small little
glass figurine of a boy.

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.434
-Uh-huh.

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:15.801
-A little boy looking out
towards the horizon,

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:20.167
seeing Christmas coming
and maybe the fattened goose.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:21.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.200
-He's looking at the goose.
-He's looking at the goose.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.167
And the goose
is looking back at him,

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.634
knowing that his goose
is cooked.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.300
But, anyway, I digress.
-Wow.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.801
-The whole point is --
-Yeah. What is the trick?

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:34.601
The whole point is I'm going
to make this disappear,

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:36.100
and you're not going to know
where it is.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.300
-This is what
I'm talking about.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.367
-Okay?
-Thank you very much.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.367
-You're very welcome. Magic Day.
Here we go.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:44.300
-Uh-huh.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.901
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:47.767
[Muffled]
Now, where is it?

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:51.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:54.667
Go ahead. Pick a hand.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.200
-Right hand!
-Either hand.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.968
-Which one?
-Right hand!

00:04:57.968 --> 00:05:00.634
-The right hand. They think
it's in the right hand.

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:02.200
[ Laughs ]

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.467
-Ha ha ha ha ha!
-Not there.

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:07.534
How about the left hand?

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:08.801
-No.

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.033
[ Cackles ]

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:11.801
I did it! I did it!

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:14.100
[ Laughs ]

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you. Thank you.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.634
Alright. Let's give you
one more chance.

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:20.133
Let's give you one more chance.
You're just warming up.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:22.067
-Okay.
-I'm gonna put the little boy --

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:24.434
You remember him from Christmas?
-Yes.

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:27.000
-I'm gonna put him
behind my back.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.634
-Okay.
-I'm going to let my hands

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:30.701
do a little something here

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:33.200
and talk to each other
a little bit.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.701
[ Speaking gibberish ]

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:40.167
[ Glass shatters ]

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.601
-I think --
-No, no. What?! What?!

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:44.267
-I think --
-Yeah!

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.067
-I think you dropped
something on the floor.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.300
It broke.
I just heard something break.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.634
-I didn't hear anything break.
-Yeah.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:51.934
-Oh, ho, ho!

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.300
My goodness!

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.467
♪ It's Magic Day! ♪

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:58.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:00.667
Is it midnight yet?

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:02.968
Because I've got to
catch a [bleep] train.

00:06:02.968 --> 00:06:04.534
-Alright. Hey, now...

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:07.000
-[Bleep]

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.067
♪ Same old game
on the [bleep] train ♪

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:11.300
♪ [Bleep] train, [bleep] train ♪

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.467
♪ Same old game
on the [bleep] train ♪

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:15.667
♪ [Bleep] train, [bleep] train ♪

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:17.968
♪ Same old game
on the [bleep] train ♪

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:19.267
-Why are they clapping?

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:21.667
-Hoo hoo hoo!
[ Laughing ]

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:25.267
-Why is everyone clapping?
The Great Bonito, everybody!

00:06:25.267 --> 00:06:27.601
-♪ [Bleep] train,
[bleep] train ♪

00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:29.834
♪ Same old game
on the [bleep] train ♪

00:06:29.834 --> 00:06:32.000
-Thank you. Thank you.
Great Benito.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.133
There he goes. Oh, my God. No!

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:36.634
-[Bleep]
-Alright. There he goes.

00:06:36.634 --> 00:06:39.767
The Great Bonito, everybody.
Oh, my gosh.

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:41.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:46.868
♪♪

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:49.667
Wow. There he goes.

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:53.167
Terrible. Terrible magician.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.400
Absolutely terrible magician.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.634
Let's do another one here.

00:06:57.634 --> 00:06:59.734
I don't even know that song,
but we all clapped to it.

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:02.100
This one's from Nina Rafferty.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.367
"Hey, Jimmy.
I love the movie 'Halloween.'

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:08.067
Is there any way you could make
a TikTok video based on it?"

00:07:08.067 --> 00:07:10.767
Yeah, sure.
Here are some clips

00:07:10.767 --> 00:07:13.167
from the movie "Halloween" that
we made into a TikTok video.

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:15.300
Here we go.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.033
-Happy Halloween!

00:07:18.033 --> 00:07:19.601
Bye!

00:07:19.601 --> 00:07:21.634
Happy Halloween!

00:07:21.634 --> 00:07:22.901
Bye!

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:25.934
Happy Halloween!
Happy, happy Halloween!

00:07:25.934 --> 00:07:28.167
♪♪

00:07:28.167 --> 00:07:29.367
Bye.

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:30.767
-Oh.

00:07:30.767 --> 00:07:32.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:32.701 --> 00:07:35.601
"Happy Halloween! Bye!"

00:07:35.601 --> 00:07:38.667
We're down
to our last suggestion.

00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:40.467
This is from Jim Randall.

00:07:40.467 --> 00:07:42.868
Says, "Hey, Jimmy,
I love Timothée Chalamet,

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:45.267
but I have so much trouble
spelling his name.

00:07:45.267 --> 00:07:47.367
Do you think you and the Roots
could write a song

00:07:47.367 --> 00:07:49.734
that would help me learn
to spell it?"

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.534
That's a great idea.
I think we can do that.

00:07:51.534 --> 00:07:53.067
Roots, hit it.

00:07:53.067 --> 00:07:57.000
♪♪

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.267
-♪ Timmy Chalamet
is the best in the game ♪

00:07:59.267 --> 00:08:01.667
-♪ But how the heck
do you spell his name? ♪

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:04.033
♪ Just take a sec,
and you might agree ♪

00:08:04.033 --> 00:08:06.534
-♪ It's easy to do,
just listen to me ♪

00:08:12.067 --> 00:08:14.234
-♪ Timothée Chalamet ♪
-♪ This is how you spell ♪

00:08:14.234 --> 00:08:15.868
-♪ Timothée Chalamet ♪

00:08:15.868 --> 00:08:18.200
-♪ Well, first you take a T
then you add an I ♪

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.701
-♪ And then M-O-T,
then an H comes by ♪

00:08:20.701 --> 00:08:22.968
-♪ Next, you add an E to an E
to match ♪

00:08:22.968 --> 00:08:25.667
-♪ We're almost done ♪
-♪ Yeah, that's the first half ♪

00:08:25.667 --> 00:08:27.868
-♪ New word up,
so you add a space ♪

00:08:27.868 --> 00:08:30.467
-♪ And slap a C
in that first letter place ♪

00:08:32.534 --> 00:08:34.934
-♪ In the last letter place,
you're gonna want a T ♪

00:08:34.934 --> 00:08:36.234
♪ And that's ♪

00:08:41.567 --> 00:08:42.834
-♪ This is how you spell ♪

00:08:44.868 --> 00:08:46.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:46.834 --> 00:08:49.767
-That's all the time we have
for Audience Suggestion Box.

00:08:49.767 --> 00:08:52.801
